  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MMR100249- EQR DEC Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will deliver a multi-sectoral Phase 2 response over 12&#x2013;18 months, targeting earthquake-affected communities in Myanmar, with an estimated reach of 15,000&#x2013;20,000 people._x000d_
_x000d_
Education (~40% of budget): Rehabilitation of damaged learning spaces and temporary learning facilities to restore safe, continuous education for children, including girls and children with disabilities. Schools will be rebuilt using hazard-resilient approaches, aligned with the Comprehensive School Safety Framework, ensuring safer learning environments and continuity planning._x000d_
_x000d_
WASH (~30% of budget): Rehabilitation and construction of gender- and disability-inclusive WASH facilities in schools and communities, incorporating climate-resilient design (e.g. flood-adapted structures, safe siting). Hygiene promotion will support improved health outcomes and reduce disease risks._x000d_
_x000d_
Resilience and Anticipatory Action (~20% of budget): Development of a cyclone-focused Anticipatory Action Framework in Mandalay and Inle Lake, including community training, early warning systems, and pre-agreed early actions to reduce the impact of future shocks._x000d_
_x000d_
Protection, Gender and Inclusion (mainstreamed, ~10%): Integrated across all sectors, ensuring targeted support to the most vulnerable groups, including girls, children with disabilities, and marginalised households, alongside safe and accessible programming._x000d_
_x000d_
The programme will be delivered in partnership with local actors, strengthening local capacity and ensuring sustainability, while integrating environmental considerations across all sectors to reduce future climate and disaster risks.</narrative>
  </description>
